A RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) pipeline. Style: architecture.

Components and flow:
1. User submits a query
2. Query goes to an Embedding Model to generate a query vector
3. Query vector is sent to a Vector Store (e.g. Pinecone) which returns top-k relevant chunks
4. Retrieved chunks plus the original query are passed to an LLM (e.g. GPT-4)
5. LLM generates a final answer returned to the User

Offline ingestion path (shown separately below the main flow):
- PDF / Documents → Text Chunker → Embedding Model → Vector Store
